    <DataNode elementId="AT4G26220-MONOMER" textLabel="Probable caffeoyl-CoA O-methyltransferase At4g26220" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9C5D7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The |FRAME: AT4G26220 CCoAOMT7| (AT4G26220) gene of |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col| belongs to a group of Mg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;-dependent low molecular weight (2327 kDa) methyltransferases with a preference for caffeoyl coenzyme A esters known as CCoAOMTs. The gene was cloned and functionally expressed in |FRAME: TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;|, and the recombinant protein was purified to homogeneity |CITS: [23416302]|. The purified protein was able to methylate |FRAME: CAFFEOYL-COA &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-caffeoyl-CoA| as expected, but was much more active with |FRAME: 5734-TETRAHYDROXYFLAVONE luteolin| (3-fold) and |FRAME: CPD-520 quercetin| (2-fold). The enzyme was also active with the flavanone |FRAME: CPD-6994 (2S)-eriodictyol| (at half the activity with |FRAME: CAFFEOYL-COA &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-caffeoyl-CoA|). Rather unusally, the enzyme could methylate this substrate at either the 3&apos; or 4&apos; positions,forming |FRAME: CPD-7071 homoeriodictyol| and |FRAME: CPD-7072 (2S)-hesperetin|, respectively |CITS: [23416302]|. The was used as part of an engineered pathway for the production of |FRAME: SCOPOLETIN scopoletin| |CITS: [23644174]|. The recombinant E. coli strain was able to produce 6.6 mg/L |FRAME: SCOPOLETIN scopoletin| in 60 h when 1 mM |FRAME: CPD-676 &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-caffeate| was fed, indicating that the enzyme is functional &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; and can utilize the |FRAME: TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;| endogenous |FRAME: S-ADENOSYLMETHIONINE &lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-adenosyl-L-methionine| as the methyl donor.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G26220-MONOMER" />
